- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/fillconnected.html
- Summary (EN): Fill Connected flood-fills a connected region of a layer, starting at a seed pixel and spreading to neighbors whose values stay within a set tolerance. It replaces the flooded area with a constant value taken from a parameter or from an input image.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Fill Connected remplit une région connexe d'une couche à partir d'un pixel germe, dans une tolérance de valeur donnée.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to flood", "fillvalue: optional layer supplying the fill color", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaling the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Seed Location: image coordinate where the flood starts", "Tolerance: maximum pixel-value difference from the seed that the fill can spread across", "Fall Off: ramp adjusting the fill alpha according to how closely pixels match the seed value", "Mask: blend amount from 0 to 1; default 1 uses only the new value", "Source: Value (Color or ID), Image Location, First Pixel or Last Pixel of the fillvalue input, or Source Location setting the sampling point in that input"]

- Caveats: ["Fall Off can reduce the fill intensity, but connectivity itself is binary: the fill is all or nothing when determining connectivity"]

